# Chrome Mox: the imprint is a link to one object (CR 607.2a), and an object that leaves and returns is a new one
# (CR 400.7). Bot1 imprints the Counterspell on turn 1. On turn 2 Bot2 bounces the Mox with Brazen Borrower's Petty Theft
# (Mox Jet and an Island pay {1}{U}). On turn 3 Bot1 casts the Mox again, a new object whose enters trigger asks again,
# and imprints the Lightning Bolt this time. The Counterspell stays in exile but is no longer this Mox's: it taps for
# red, the Bolt's color, and blue is refused.

[Bot1 Deck]
Chrome Mox
Counterspell
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Jet
Brazen Borrower
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Chrome Mox.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Counterspell)
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Brazen Borrower.Cast(Chrome Mox; Ability: Adventure)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Chrome Mox.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Chrome Mox.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Chrome Mox.Activate(Color: Red)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Brazen Borrower; Counterspell; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield = Chrome Mox
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Island
